# core.autocrlf is unreliable on this project's dev machine: a global
# `false` overrides a system-level `true`, so git does not normalise line
# endings on `git add` and whatever CRLF/LF mix lands in the working tree
# gets committed verbatim. Pin normalization here instead, so correctness
# doesn't depend on per-machine git config.
* text=auto eol=lf
